 prescribed or controlled burns and brush clearing.","end":7976,"id":"7708bdd740cb3d2482aeea3a1b254bc2c6ddb345951889afc73db6f89f13415c","manager":true,"party":"R","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-21/html/CREC-2026-04-21-pt1-PgH3013.htm#:~:text=The%20FIRE%20Act%20ensures%20that%20States%20are%20not%20penalized%20for%20wildfire%20mitigation%20practices%20like%20prescribed%20or%20controlled%20burns%20and%20brush%20clearing.","quote":"The FIRE Act ensures that States are not penalized for wildfire \nmitigation practices like prescribed or controlled burns and brush \nclearing.","sha256":"38c542ad120c850cfa240af6196212182bab6d742e0b0289f78872db96111d07","side":"Yea","speaker":"Gary J. Palmer","start":7834,"state":"AL","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-21/html/CREC-2026-04-21-pt1-PgH3013.htm"},{"bio":"P000034","display":"Republicans are peddling this dangerous bill as an attempt to promote prescribed burns and combat wildfires. As has been true for the other dirty bills that we considered over the last week or so, this bill fails to address the stated goal and instead provides overly broad exemptions to the Clean Air Act that will harm American families and children.","end":10606,"id":"8b81677ad6cba9ec2edb8baf04a8c78294c70865a263726d01c74cff23447c31","manager":true,"party":"D","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-21/html/CREC-2026-04-21-pt1-PgH3013.htm#:~:text=Republicans%20are%20peddling%20this%20dangerous%20bill%20as%20an%20attempt%20to%20promote%20prescribed%20burns%20and%20combat%20wildfires.%20As%20has%20been%20true%20for%20the%20other%20dirty%20bills%20that%20we%20considered%20over%20the%20last%20week%20or%20so%2C%20this%20bill%20fails%20to%20address%20the%20stated%20goal%20and%20instead%20provides%20overly%20broad%20exemptions%20to%20the%20Clean%20Air%20Act%20that%20will%20harm%20American%20families%20and%20children.","quote":"Republicans are peddling this dangerous bill as an attempt to promote \nprescribed burns and combat wildfires. As has been true for the other \ndirty bills that we considered over the last week or so, this bill \nfails to address the stated goal and instead provides overly broad \nexemptions to the Clean Air Act that will harm American families and \nchildren.","sha256":"38c542ad120c850cfa240af6196212182bab6d742e0b0289f78872db96111d07","side":"Nay","speaker":"Frank Pallone, Jr.","start":10249,"state":"NJ","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-21/html/CREC-2026-04-21-pt1-PgH3013.htm"}],"sources":{"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-21/html/CREC-2026-04-21-pt1-PgH3013.htm":"38c542ad120c850cfa240af6196212182bab6d742e0b0289f78872db96111d07","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-22/html/CREC-2026-04-22-pt1-PgH3064.htm":"37137b2f84cc0f6bc59e9f73fe5c0c61cbea55c6622fcdbab16b3d0f3b9032a1"},"vote":"house:119:2:136"},"house:119:2:137":{"bill":"119-hr-5587","date":"2026-04-23","floorDebate":["https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm"],"passage":{"nay":186,"result":"Passed","sha256":"c2c0806d427a081fd26a552d57dc5822dfee8b7b7fdccbd46a7e650415457305","url":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll137.xml","yea":231},"points":[{"bio":"W000821","display":"Crucially, this bill upholds strong environmental standards by stipulating that Federal requirements may only be waived if operators receive drilling permits and comply with historic preservation laws on the State level. Notably, the bill would not impact the royalties paid to the Federal Government. Therefore, it will not reduce the Federal revenues generated by geothermal production.","end":7318,"id":"bdabae4c908f145f3f567f6e7d02f471874252dba88a07fd7b076d49a685c9e1","manager":true,"party":"R","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm#:~:text=Crucially%2C%20this%20bill%20upholds%20strong%20environmental%20standards%20by%20stipulating%20that%20Federal%20requirements%20may%20only%20be%20waived%20if%20operators%20receive%20drilling%20permits%20and%20comply%20with%20historic%20preservation%20laws%20on%20the%20State%20level.%20Notably%2C%20the%20bill%20would%20not%20impact%20the%20royalties%20paid%20to%20the%20Federal%20Government.%20Therefore%2C%20it%20will%20not%20reduce%20the%20Federal%20revenues%20generated%20by%20geothermal%20production.","quote":"Crucially, this bill upholds strong environmental standards by \nstipulating that Federal requirements may only be waived if operators \nreceive drilling permits and comply with historic preservation laws on \nthe State level.\n  Notably, the bill would not impact the royalties paid to the Federal \nGovernment. Therefore, it will not reduce the Federal revenues \ngenerated by geothermal production.","sha256":"e62c69298e1c6b1fef018ddc4abbaf3fca6e5364780c5746432e738238750a64","side":"Yea","speaker":"Bruce Westerman","start":6923,"state":"AR","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm"},{"bio":"K000397","display":"The HEATS Act fixes that by cutting red tape and waiving Federal drilling permit requirements for geothermal wells on State and local lands. Operators will still go through a rigorous State-level permitting process, but they will no longer be subjected to duplicative Federal requirements that slow production, raise costs, and kill jobs.","end":16611,"id":"b4b8b4db96bc3d843a6f1a8880c9d2fa6f31ba60f56a57977bb07c5873041c5a","manager":false,"party":"R","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm#:~:text=The%20HEATS%20Act%20fixes%20that%20by%20cutting%20red%20tape%20and%20waiving%20Federal%20drilling%20permit%20requirements%20for%20geothermal%20wells%20on%20State%20and%20local%20lands.%20Operators%20will%20still%20go%20through%20a%20rigorous%20State%2Dlevel%20permitting%20process%2C%20but%20they%20will%20no%20longer%20be%20subjected%20to%20duplicative%20Federal%20requirements%20that%20slow%20production%2C%20raise%20costs%2C%20and%20kill%20jobs.","quote":"The HEATS Act fixes that by cutting red tape and waiving Federal \ndrilling permit requirements for geothermal wells on State and local \nlands. Operators will still go through a rigorous State-level \npermitting process, but they will no longer be subjected to duplicative \nFederal requirements that slow production, raise costs, and kill jobs.","sha256":"e62c69298e1c6b1fef018ddc4abbaf3fca6e5364780c5746432e738238750a64","side":"Yea","speaker":"Young Kim","start":16269,"state":"CA","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm"},{"bio":"A000381","display":"even good energy sources need good permitting policy. I am a strong supporter of geothermal energy, but the HEATS Act could undermine the on-the-ground support and good environmental track record geothermal currently enjoys.","end":25564,"id":"cdf3f5f00542e6fd649c65eb4965847dcdb680bcd9c3da31616ccdbf4c806354","manager":true,"party":"D","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm#:~:text=Mr.%20Speaker%2C%20in%20closing%2C%20even%20good%20energy%20sources%20need%20good%20permitting%20policy.%20I%20am%20a%20strong%20supporter%20of%20geothermal%20energy%2C%20but%20the%20HEATS%20Act%20could%20undermine%20the%20on%2Dthe%2Dground%20support%20and%20good%20environmental%20track%20record%20geothermal%20currently%20enjoys.","quote":"Mr. Speaker, in closing, even good energy sources need good \npermitting policy. I am a strong supporter of geothermal energy, but \nthe HEATS Act could undermine the on-the-ground support and good \nenvironmental track record geothermal currently enjoys.","sha256":"e62c69298e1c6b1fef018ddc4abbaf3fca6e5364780c5746432e738238750a64","side":"Nay","speaker":"Yassamin Ansari","start":25312,"state":"AZ","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm"},{"bio":"H001068","display":"While this may sound innocuous--oh, it is just subsurface; it is below what we can see with our eyes--without a Federal permit, the core safeguards for development affecting Federal resources would totally disappear. That includes protections under the National Environmental Policy Act, the National Historic Preservation Act, and the Endangered Species Act.","end":19292,"id":"04d50b5511a8b5796d62a25e9e3d8fe02b821b2170960d81a3b6dfba8ffd55ea","manager":false,"party":"D","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm#:~:text=While%20this%20may%20sound%20innocuous%2D%2Doh%2C%20it%20is%20just%20subsurface%3B%20it%20is%20below%20what%20we%20can%20see%20with%20our%20eyes%2D%2Dwithout%20a%20Federal%20permit%2C%20the%20core%20safeguards%20for%20development%20affecting%20Federal%20resources%20would%20totally%20disappear.%20That%20includes%20protections%20under%20the%20National%20Environmental%20Policy%20Act%2C%20the%20National%20Historic%20Preservation%20Act%2C%20and%20the%20Endangered%20Species%20Act.","quote":"While this may sound innocuous--oh, it is just subsurface; it is \nbelow what we can see with our eyes--without a Federal permit, the core \nsafeguards for development affecting Federal resources would totally \ndisappear. That includes protections under the National Environmental \nPolicy Act, the National Historic Preservation Act, and the Endangered \nSpecies Act.","sha256":"e62c69298e1c6b1fef018ddc4abbaf3fca6e5364780c5746432e738238750a64","side":"Nay","speaker":"Jared Huffman","start":18928,"state":"CA","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm"}],"sources":{"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm":"e62c69298e1c6b1fef018ddc4abbaf3fca6e5364780c5746432e738238750a64"},"vote":"house:119:2:137"},"house:119:2:154":{"bill":"119-hr-7567","date":"2026-04-30","floorDebate":["https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-29/html/CREC-2026-04-29-pt1-PgH3169.htm","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-30/html/CREC-2026-04-30-pt1-PgH3311.htm"],"passage":{"nay":200,"result":"Passed","sha256":"76642e459dd4f0759c68c08b018b1272cde006984922795c83cbe827cdbda1b0","url":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll154.xml","yea":224},"points":[],"sources":{"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-29/html/CREC-2026-04-29-pt1-PgH3169.htm":"8c6766da1ad79d27e2ee5d149d77e55bf6ff4467363bcad2c5153591142c17f6","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-30/html/CREC-2026-04-30-pt1-PgH3311.htm":"4e8fdb6b5516521c672933956ee202ac7b2e66200b6cae34cdea20e54151509a"},"vote":"house:119:2:154"},"house:119:2:164":{"bill":"119-hr-1346","date":"2026-05-13","floorDebate":["https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-13/html/CREC-2026-05-13-pt1-PgH3421.htm","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-13/html/CREC-2026-05-13-pt1-PgH3435.htm"],"passage":{"nay":203,"result":"Passed","sha256":"784496f77a4e51ff763d7c44685c04a9af96fac1d227718fbcbbd164cf10d6aa","url":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll164.xml","yea":218},"points":[{"bio":"G000558","display":"The underlying bill will allow for year-round sale of 15 percent ethanol and gasoline, which farmers say is needed to provide an additional market for their crops without impacting air quality.","end":18565,"id":"2f9affa78d14d3a4425c5669234d3f4a2c997dd5062f406bf0313716b799e8dd","manager":false,"party":"R","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-13/html/CREC-2026-05-13-pt1-PgH3421.htm#:~:text=The%20underlying%20bill%20will%20allow%20for%20year%2Dround%20sale%20of%2015%20percent%20ethanol%20and%20gasoline%2C%20which%20farmers%20say%20is%20needed%20to%20provide%20an%20additional%20market%20for%20their%20crops%20without%20impacting%20air%20quality.","quote":"The underlying bill will allow for year-round sale of 15 percent \nethanol and gasoline, which farmers say is needed to provide an \nadditional market for their crops without impacting air quality.","sha256":"5149758b88a3838ceedf62d46275c68f4eee6c2dc80f6dac1d6b62dc0889d58b","side":"Yea","speaker":"Brett Guthrie","start":18370,"state":"KY","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-13/html/CREC-2026-05-13-pt1-PgH3421.htm"},{"bio":"F000482","display":"E15 is homegrown American energy. Most importantly, eliminating the artificial prohibition on summer sales of E15 is an important step toward creating the consistent demand that will allow this industry to grow and stand on its own without RFS one day. We have to get this done first.","end":31753,"id":"17812993b7052cdc2358c6ee55d3e67f971eb6306005d4dc58e55d2a884cab76","manager":false,"party":"R","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-13/html/CREC-2026-05-13-pt1-PgH3421.htm#:~:text=E15%20is%20homegrown%20American%20energy.%20Most%20importantly%2C%20eliminating%20the%20artificial%20prohibition%20on%20summer%20sales%20of%20E15%20is%20an%20important%20step%20toward%20creating%20the%20consistent%20demand%20that%20will%20allow%20this%20industry%20to%20grow%20and%20stand%20on%20its%20own%20without%20RFS%20one%20day.%20We%20have%20to%20get%20this%20done%20first.","quote":"E15 is homegrown American energy. Most importantly, eliminating the \nartificial prohibition on summer sales of E15 is an important step \ntoward creating the consistent demand that will allow this industry to \ngrow and stand on its own without RFS one day.\n  We have to get this done first.","sha256":"5149758b88a3838ceedf62d46275c68f4eee6c2dc80f6dac1d6b62dc0889d58b","side":"Yea","speaker":"Julie Fedorchak","start":31464,"state":"ND","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-13/html/CREC-2026-05-13-pt1-PgH3421.htm"},{"bio":"H001096","display":"This bill is disastrous for Wyoming refiners and independent petroleum producers, leading to a direct loss of at least 750 jobs in my home State.","end":45643,"id":"dd1361800695c213f5e270787f5bca966e5529d23d41f28504ec375d61281e51","manager":false,"party":"R","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-13/html/CREC-2026-05-13-pt1-PgH3421.htm#:~:text=This%20bill%20is%20disastrous%20for%20Wyoming%20refiners%20and%20independent%20petroleum%20producers%2C%20leading%20to%20a%20direct%20loss%20of%20at%20least%20750%20jobs%20in%20my%20home%20State.","quote":"This bill is disastrous for Wyoming refiners and independent \npetroleum producers, leading to a direct loss of at least 750 jobs in \nmy home State.","sha256":"5149758b88a3838ceedf62d46275c68f4eee6c2dc80f6dac1d6b62dc0889d58b","side":"Nay","speaker":"Harriet M. Hageman","start":45496,"state":"WY","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-13/html/CREC-2026-05-13-pt1-PgH3421.htm"},{"bio":"R000614","display":"Expanding E15 is just the wrong direction to go. It is going to harm refiners. It is going to drive up the cost of gas.","end":58242,"id":"a5773e415131f9d506441d3f6b99fe1c585363057e5b82e18e363b626801602e","manager":false,"party":"R","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-13/html/CREC-2026-05-13-pt1-PgH3421.htm#:~:text=Expanding%20E15%20is%20just%20the%20wrong%20direction%20to%20go.%20It%20is%20going%20to%20harm%20refiners.%20It%20is%20going%20to%20drive%20up%20the%20cost%20of%20gas.","quote":"Expanding E15 is just the wrong direction to go. \nIt is going to harm refiners. It is going to drive up the cost of gas.","sha256":"5149758b88a3838ceedf62d46275c68f4eee6c2dc80f6dac1d6b62dc0889d58b","side":"Nay","speaker":"Chip Roy","start":58122,"state":"TX","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-13/html/CREC-2026-05-13-pt1-PgH3421.htm"}],"sources":{"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-13/html/CREC-2026-05-13-pt1-PgH3421.htm":"5149758b88a3838ceedf62d46275c68f4eee6c2dc80f6dac1d6b62dc0889d58b","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-13/html/CREC-2026-05-13-pt1-PgH3435.htm":"c7a249b219cbdf8f30c1adf4119e90563480c985593d77b91c006de2a482af4b"},"vote":"house:119:2:164"},"house:119:2:171":{"bill":"119-hr-5625","date":"2026-05-14","floorDebate":["https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-14/html/CREC-2026-05-14-pt1-PgH3471-3.htm","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-14/html/CREC-2026-05-14-pt1-PgH3507.htm"],"passage":{"nay":116,"result":"Passed","sha256":"3ddf57d28b95c50c37a89f751224bab66d427a8b5507cf1a6ae957ba528006ce","url":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll171.xml","yea":308},"points":[],"sources":{"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-14/html/CREC-2026-05-14-pt1-PgH3471-3.htm":"dc5889986328dd40d3e5702695e69926e1feab6c11792c58546ba6ad0b51c083","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-14/html/CREC-2026-05-14-pt1-PgH3507.htm":"506b65181d0c996d710163fddbee0161f766fe052af546d7c24b8ebfe343f099"},"vote":"house:119:2:171"},"house:119:2:188":{"bill":"119-hr-1329","date":"2026-05-21","floorDebate":["https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3692.htm","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3707-4.htm"],"passage":{"nay":216,"result":"Failed","sha256":"9d45b832d5380ca3400ecc465f933d45f88130eb67f92f7c9dd9cb4833390c03","url":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll188.xml","yea":204},"points":[{"bio":"S001213","display":"It has been 250 years since we declared independence. As we celebrate this milestone, I think it is all the more worthy that we pass this bill and begin construction of the museum dedicated to the history of American women. Throughout our history, women have played a pivotal role in so many of our Nation's most celebrated achievements and innovations.","end":10418,"id":"be1990fe84f2250724c405ef5b784e41893769bcaf785f2f7502d3ed45ee057a","manager":false,"party":"R","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3692.htm#:~:text=It%20has%20been%20250%20years%20since%20we%20declared%20independence.%20As%20we%20celebrate%20this%20milestone%2C%20I%20think%20it%20is%20all%20the%20more%20worthy%20that%20we%20pass%20this%20bill%20and%20begin%20construction%20of%20the%20museum%20dedicated%20to%20the%20history%20of%20American%20women.%20Throughout%20our%20history%2C%20women%20have%20played%20a%20pivotal%20role%20in%20so%20many%20of%20our%20Nation%27s%20most%20celebrated%20achievements%20and%20innovations.","quote":"It has been 250 years \nsince we declared independence. As we celebrate this milestone, I think \nit is all the more worthy that we pass this bill and begin construction \nof the museum dedicated to the history of American women.\n  Throughout our history, women have played a pivotal role in so many \nof our Nation's most celebrated achievements and innovations.","sha256":"57bc674f0374c7c835ee5706713c8d2ea3dcb96c3beb56478aa33bbafe8c361d","side":"Yea","speaker":"Bryan Steil","start":10059,"state":"WI","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3692.htm"},{"bio":"T000472","display":"I rise in opposition to this amended bill. I was a proud cosponsor of the bill, as introduced. Yet, instead of moving the bipartisan text, Republicans have hijacked this bill to give President Trump complete and total authority over the Smithsonian American Women's History Museum's location.","end":24567,"id":"19bc1421f7c391e8a9004679c1aaaddb887cfbe6e9d74e24a4913ebf6126792c","manager":false,"party":"D","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3692.htm#:~:text=Mr.%20Speaker%2C%20I%20rise%20in%20opposition%20to%20this%20amended%20bill.%20I%20was%20a%20proud%20cosponsor%20of%20the%20bill%2C%20as%20introduced.%20Yet%2C%20instead%20of%20moving%20the%20bipartisan%20text%2C%20Republicans%20have%20hijacked%20this%20bill%20to%20give%20President%20Trump%20complete%20and%20total%20authority%20over%20the%20Smithsonian%20American%20Women%27s%20History%20Museum%27s%20location.","quote":"Mr. Speaker, I rise in opposition to this amended bill. I \nwas a proud cosponsor of the bill, as introduced. Yet, instead of \nmoving the bipartisan text, Republicans have hijacked this bill to give \nPresident Trump complete and total authority over the Smithsonian \nAmerican Women's History Museum's location.","sha256":"57bc674f0374c7c835ee5706713c8d2ea3dcb96c3beb56478aa33bbafe8c361d","side":"Nay","speaker":"Mark Takano","start":24258,"state":"CA","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3692.htm"}],"sources":{"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3692.htm":"57bc674f0374c7c835ee5706713c8d2ea3dcb96c3beb56478aa33bbafe8c361d","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3707-4.htm":"fcf3dddb5d03bad97ae8870bdd06726dc19327a449c7f072aefb1b0b64c080a4"},"vote":"house:119:2:188"},"house:119:2:190":{"bill":"119-hr-1041","date":"2026-05-21","floorDebate":["https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3684-5.htm","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3710-2.htm"],"passage":{"nay":201,"result":"Passed","sha256":"805c1ca5e6f2d9fd3a1f037ac9fb246895ec6ad3d0e28dfe30de51a75f9c629f","url":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll190.xml","yea":216},"points":[{"bio":"E000246","display":"This bill is about basic fairness and restoring a standard that respects both our veterans and the Constitution. Under current practice, a veteran who simply needs help managing their VA benefits can be reported to the FBI's background check system and lose their Second Amendment rights without ever appearing before a judge.","end":46526,"id":"8a44399dab9c640d3b80903945ba6f7887d7a4fc7bdb1453c720000b25888bca","manager":false,"party":"R","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3684-5.htm#:~:text=This%20bill%20is%20about%20basic%20fairness%20and%20restoring%20a%20standard%20that%20respects%20both%20our%20veterans%20and%20the%20Constitution.%20Under%20current%20practice%2C%20a%20veteran%20who%20simply%20needs%20help%20managing%20their%20VA%20benefits%20can%20be%20reported%20to%20the%20FBI%27s%20background%20check%20system%20and%20lose%20their%20Second%20Amendment%20rights%20without%20ever%20appearing%20before%20a%20judge.","quote":"This bill is about basic fairness and restoring a standard that \nrespects both our veterans and the Constitution. Under current \npractice, a veteran who simply needs help managing their VA benefits \ncan be reported to the FBI's background check system and lose their \nSecond Amendment rights without ever appearing before a judge.","sha256":"2253d263eb9c613b463b3630b22b7ed66eb811bf5b71ed067c49776ca2cf3c88","side":"Yea","speaker":"Chuck Edwards","start":46196,"state":"NC","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3684-5.htm"},{"bio":"W000797","display":"Every day, 17 veterans die by suicide, and 13 of them use a firearm to take their lives. That number is simply unacceptable to me, as I know it is to all of my colleagues, but I am deeply concerned that, with this bill, we are about to make it worse.","end":26968,"id":"acf08eda89381facc17cf46540c18d03801f7817a14946c82128d5383ab39d86","manager":false,"party":"D","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3684-5.htm#:~:text=Every%20day%2C%2017%20veterans%20die%20by%20suicide%2C%20and%2013%20of%20them%20use%20a%20firearm%20to%20take%20their%20lives.%20That%20number%20is%20simply%20unacceptable%20to%20me%2C%20as%20I%20know%20it%20is%20to%20all%20of%20my%20colleagues%2C%20but%20I%20am%20deeply%20concerned%20that%2C%20with%20this%20bill%2C%20we%20are%20about%20to%20make%20it%20worse.","quote":"Every day, 17 veterans die by suicide, and 13 of them use a firearm \nto take their lives. That number is simply unacceptable to me, as I \nknow it is to all of my colleagues, but I am deeply concerned that, \nwith this bill, we are about to make it worse.","sha256":"2253d263eb9c613b463b3630b22b7ed66eb811bf5b71ed067c49776ca2cf3c88","side":"Nay","speaker":"Debbie Wasserman Schultz","start":26715,"state":"FL","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3684-5.htm"}],"sources":{"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3684-5.htm":"2253d263eb9c613b463b3630b22b7ed66eb811bf5b71ed067c49776ca2cf3c88","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3710-2.htm":"5194de8aa9c77a99bad74bd27ee52834d9abcdc514d413c87b1153b54c5b7e3a"},"vote":"house:119:2:190"},"house:119:2:191":{"bill":"119-hr-6047","date":"2026-05-21","floorDebate":["https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3699.htm","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3711.htm"],"passage":{"nay":179,"result":"Passed","sha256":"b910a7edc72b36e0e17fd3f3ab384a6225d3f24b0d7d52490a5d7acd0c12351e","url":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll191.xml","yea":235},"points":[{"bio":"B001295","display":"This legislation would provide the first meaningful increase in survivor benefits for families like Brileys since 1993. Over 500,000 survivors like Sharri receive Dependency and Indemnity Compensation from the VA.","end":12297,"id":"e5f9a72860f26974b2b6baba46a2434699bc16104274bd52d1ead78b832a8475","manager":true,"party":"R","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3699.htm#:~:text=This%20legislation%20would%20provide%20the%20first%20meaningful%20increase%20in%20survivor%20benefits%20for%20families%20like%20Brileys%20since%201993.%20Over%20500%2C000%20survivors%20like%20Sharri%20receive%20Dependency%20and%20Indemnity%20Compensation%20from%20the%20VA.","quote":"This legislation would provide the first meaningful increase in \nsurvivor benefits for families like Brileys since 1993.\n  Over 500,000 survivors like Sharri receive Dependency and Indemnity \nCompensation from the VA.","sha256":"462e41fd72024aa8158950609018a4038ceeda7bd801ba680952718e6b504e18","side":"Yea","speaker":"Mike Bost","start":12080,"state":"IL","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3699.htm"},{"bio":"T000472","display":"Representative Barrett and House Republicans have engineered here an impossible choice. What they have said to the American people is that only by raising costs on one set of veterans can we afford to help another.","end":31488,"id":"348703cc85ec1cece7df32d7a2cf7fdfac54898e7fc0a3ed41e9294636f4a507","manager":true,"party":"D","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3699.htm#:~:text=Representative%20Barrett%20and%20House%20Republicans%20have%20engineered%20here%20an%20impossible%20choice.%20What%20they%20have%20said%20to%20the%20American%20people%20is%20that%20only%20by%20raising%20costs%20on%20one%20set%20of%20veterans%20can%20we%20afford%20to%20help%20another.","quote":"Representative Barrett and House Republicans have engineered here an \nimpossible choice. What they have said to the American people is that \nonly by raising costs on one set of veterans can we afford to help \nanother.","sha256":"462e41fd72024aa8158950609018a4038ceeda7bd801ba680952718e6b504e18","side":"Nay","speaker":"Mark Takano","start":31271,"state":"CA","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3699.htm"}],"sources":{"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3699.htm":"462e41fd72024aa8158950609018a4038ceeda7bd801ba680952718e6b504e18","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-05-21/html/CREC-2026-05-21-pt1-PgH3711.htm":"951ab9ee847fd84361e09fbe99a7f6825b9064e1e5ce5ecbf33f72b46712076d"},"vote":"house:119:2:191"},"house:119:2:198":{"bill":"119-hr-7726","date":"2026-06-03","floorDebate":["https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-06-03/html/CREC-2026-06-03-pt1-PgH3796.htm","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-06-03/html/CREC-2026-06-03-pt1-PgH3811.htm"],"passage":{"nay":207,"result":"Passed","sha256":"bbf66a422d855560180d71fa028542a574621d257431cba60c9c865bfffbf494","url":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll198.xml","yea":217},"points":[],"sources":{"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-06-03/html/CREC-2026-06-03-pt1-PgH3796.htm":"cb9d9c40d631cc8b8ff8ffda47f5bb03fad872b29caa5440246aaeb423dfffc0","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-06-03/html/CREC-2026-06-03-pt1-PgH3811.htm":"035f656fa2e6dee283536869b5e43c30e9e996f124fbcdc8492d86684e2a9663"},"vote":"house:119:2:198"},"house:119:2:205":{"bill":"119-hr-8646","date":"2026-06-04","floorDebate":["https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-06-04/html/CREC-2026-06-04-pt1-PgH3840-4.htm","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-06-04/html/CREC-2026-06-04-pt1-PgH3877.htm"],"passage":{"nay":210,"result":"Passed","sha256":"0219f24604a532812765ac29273877d4d65381f407d146e1ea8bab7efb0021cb","url":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll205.xml","yea":213},"points":[{"bio":"H001052","display":"For fiscal year 2027, the subcommittee's discretionary allocation is $26.27 billion, a $380 million, or 1.4 percent, decrease from fiscal year 2026 enacted levels. In a setting of $2 trillion deficits, these modest spending reductions are necessary.","end":3340,"id":"a95778d5c1b54ef280363764af9ceb9373f9a40b929df3f79367bb064608cd17","manager":true,"party":"R","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-06-04/html/CREC-2026-06-04-pt1-PgH3840-4.htm#:~:text=For%20fiscal%20year%202027%2C%20the%20subcommittee%27s%20discretionary%20allocation%20is%20%2426.27%20billion%2C%20a%20%24380%20million%2C%20or%201.4%20percent%2C%20decrease%20from%20fiscal%20year%202026%20enacted%20levels.%20In%20a%20setting%20of%20%242%20trillion%20deficits%2C%20these%20modest%20spending%20reductions%20are%20necessary.","quote":"For fiscal year 2027, the subcommittee's discretionary allocation is \n$26.27 billion, a $380 million, or 1.4 percent, decrease from fiscal \nyear 2026 enacted levels.\n  In a setting of $2 trillion deficits, these modest spending \nreductions are necessary.","sha256":"0933326172a0dea01b3f2756e169b3d1ec3283c7e42397603485982eb55f675c","side":"Yea","speaker":"Andy Harris","start":3086,"state":"MD","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-06-04/html/CREC-2026-06-04-pt1-PgH3840-4.htm"},{"bio":"B000490","display":"It makes substantial reductions across rural development, farm production and conservation, nutrition, and foreign aid programs. Most notably, House Republicans are proposing to drastically reduce fruit and vegetable benefits for 5 million low-income women, infants, and children in the WIC program.","end":8434,"id":"caf0bb86fca2e3b036b8e6d7093e6371b1a5cd0c15bb362f27bfae9b45fa95da","manager":true,"party":"D","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-06-04/html/CREC-2026-06-04-pt1-PgH3840-4.htm#:~:text=It%20makes%20substantial%20reductions%20across%20rural%20development%2C%20farm%20production%20and%20conservation%2C%20nutrition%2C%20and%20foreign%20aid%20programs.%20Most%20notably%2C%20House%20Republicans%20are%20proposing%20to%20drastically%20reduce%20fruit%20and%20vegetable%20benefits%20for%205%20million%20low%2Dincome%20women%2C%20infants%2C%20and%20children%20in%20the%20WIC%20program.","quote":"It makes substantial \nreductions across rural development, farm production and conservation, \nnutrition, and foreign aid programs.\n  Most notably, House Republicans are proposing to drastically reduce \nfruit and vegetable benefits for 5 million low-income women, infants, \nand children in the WIC program.","sha256":"0933326172a0dea01b3f2756e169b3d1ec3283c7e42397603485982eb55f675c","side":"Nay","speaker":"Sanford D. Bishop, Jr.","start":8129,"state":"GA","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2