"bio":"H001072","display":"Financial privacy is fundamental to consumer trust and confidence in our financial system. As technology continues to transform financial services, protecting Americans' financial privacy remains an essential part of Congress' oversight role.","end":9041,"id":"43a8290ccf3dd0182462cd6bede8c1367c026447a3ec27b3eb9c27fd3e8b3cf0","manager":true,"party":"R","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-14/html/CREC-2026-07-14-pt1-PgH4441-2.htm#:~:text=Financial%20privacy%20is%20fundamental%20to%20consumer%20trust%20and%20confidence%20in%20our%20financial%20system.%20As%20technology%20continues%20to%20transform%20financial%20services%2C%20protecting%20Americans%27%20financial%20privacy%20remains%20an%20essential%20part%20of%20Congress%27%20oversight%20role.","quote":"Financial privacy is fundamental to consumer trust and confidence in \nour financial system. As technology continues to transform financial \nservices, protecting Americans' financial privacy remains an essential \npart of Congress' oversight role.","sha256":"9db51bec7111484c878b597a2c658745aaddabf8544a217a28dc23cf5e6b61c7","side":"Yea","speaker":"J. French Hill","start":8796,"state":"AR","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-14/html/CREC-2026-07-14-pt1-PgH4441-2.htm"},{"bio":"T000460","display":"I rise in opposition to H.R. 1181, a bill which makes it harder to catch criminals and makes our communities less safe.","end":18872,"id":"247b307b1ee88ca8468d8e1fc1e6eacd846fbc340ac242bb2ed63606a6e8473a","manager":false,"party":"D","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-14/html/CREC-2026-07-14-pt1-PgH4441-2.htm#:~:text=Mr.%20Speaker%2C%20I%20rise%20in%20opposition%20to%20H.R.%201181%2C%20a%20bill%20which%20makes%20it%20harder%20to%20catch%20criminals%20and%20makes%20our%20communities%20less%20safe.","quote":"Mr. Speaker, I rise in opposition to H.R. 1181, a bill which makes it \nharder to catch criminals and makes our communities less safe.","sha256":"9db51bec7111484c878b597a2c658745aaddabf8544a217a28dc23cf5e6b61c7","side":"Nay","speaker":"Mike Thompson","start":18739,"state":"CA","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-14/html/CREC-2026-07-14-pt1-PgH4441-2.htm"}],"sources":{"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-14/html/CREC-2026-07-14-pt1-PgH4441-2.htm":"9db51bec7111484c878b597a2c658745aaddabf8544a217a28dc23cf5e6b61c7","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-14/html/CREC-2026-07-14-pt1-PgH4451.htm":"cf1ea2491fea5641fe3af103346f7b96c236cefd328d835b30114933509d13b1"},"vote":"house:119:2:240"},"house:119:2:247":{"bill":"119-hr-8595","date":"2026-07-15","floorDebate":["https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-15/html/CREC-2026-07-15-pt1-PgH4480.htm"],"passage":{"nay":209,"result":"Passed","sha256":"edf6dd86982bebc2283d43a3f41149789121160112327b939263ac82fd65e441","url":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll247.xml","yea":217},"points":[{"bio":"D000600","display":"The bill maintains $1.8 billion for partners in the Indo-Pacific, including $500 million in military assistance for Taiwan. It provides unwavering support for Israel and fully funds the United States-Israel Memorandum of Understanding by providing $3.3 billion in security assistance.","end":4627,"id":"e10c4d896dc182fa9ae03771b248ec965f612eedec1592a3e23df6ae3d7ff2fd","manager":true,"party":"R","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-15/html/CREC-2026-07-15-pt1-PgH4480.htm#:~:text=The%20bill%20maintains%20%241.8%20billion%20for%20partners%20in%20the%20Indo%2DPacific%2C%20including%20%24500%20million%20in%20military%20assistance%20for%20Taiwan.%20It%20provides%20unwavering%20support%20for%20Israel%20and%20fully%20funds%20the%20United%20States%2DIsrael%20Memorandum%20of%20Understanding%20by%20providing%20%243.3%20billion%20in%20security%20assistance.","quote":"The bill maintains $1.8 billion for partners in the Indo-Pacific, \nincluding $500 million in military assistance for Taiwan. It provides \nunwavering support for Israel and fully funds the United States-Israel \nMemorandum of Understanding by providing $3.3 billion in security \nassistance.","sha256":"8687efc91b5f46ae21cbe53b710d16be36466b460f17df46e0b1ee4fe9fda8b0","side":"Yea","speaker":"Mario Diaz-Balart","start":4339,"state":"FL","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-15/html/CREC-2026-07-15-pt1-PgH4480.htm"},{"bio":"H000874","display":"Sadly, this bill has zero for Ukraine, our ally fighting the Russian invader. That is a grave mistake and absolutely the wrong approach. It is a dangerous signal at a time when we ought to show unwavering support for Ukraine's defense of its homeland.","end":27803,"id":"356273a061849c7349a6b4a7ebc0a26ab5373e712fe8b6faa73fcc615a591e76","manager":false,"party":"D","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-15/html/CREC-2026-07-15-pt1-PgH4480.htm#:~:text=Sadly%2C%20this%20bill%20has%20zero%20for%20Ukraine%2C%20our%20ally%20fighting%20the%20Russian%20invader.%20That%20is%20a%20grave%20mistake%20and%20absolutely%20the%20wrong%20approach.%20It%20is%20a%20dangerous%20signal%20at%20a%20time%20when%20we%20ought%20to%20show%20unwavering%20support%20for%20Ukraine%27s%20defense%20of%20its%20homeland.","quote":"Sadly, this bill has zero for Ukraine, our ally fighting the Russian \ninvader. That is a grave mistake and absolutely the wrong approach. It \nis a dangerous signal at a time when we ought to show unwavering \nsupport for Ukraine's defense of its homeland.","sha256":"8687efc91b5f46ae21cbe53b710d16be36466b460f17df46e0b1ee4fe9fda8b0","side":"Nay","speaker":"Steny H. Hoyer","start":27549,"state":"MD","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-15/html/CREC-2026-07-15-pt1-PgH4480.htm"}],"sources":{"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-15/html/CREC-2026-07-15-pt1-PgH4480.htm":"8687efc91b5f46ae21cbe53b710d16be36466b460f17df46e0b1ee4fe9fda8b0"},"vote":"house:119:2:247"},"house:119:2:272":{"bill":"119-hr-9770","date":"2026-07-21","floorDebate":["https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-21/html/CREC-2026-07-21-pt1-PgH4731.htm","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-21/html/CREC-2026-07-21-pt1-PgH5019.htm"],"passage":{"nay":205,"result":"Passed","sha256":"c1104ec5fd295cb5fe8f4c6166bdb7d6810924c146bbba209e6bf05dfd3fee8b","url":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll272.xml","yea":220},"points":[{"bio":"C001053","display":"This Congress has a constitutional duty to fund the government. If Article I teaches us anything, it is that governing means doing the work, not waiting for a crisis. It is a responsibility I have never viewed as optional and one I have remained committed to honoring through regular order.","end":21437,"id":"0f707d8ca3c5a91890acf7d881398268f9a48dad91157d5b41baadf169da0255","manager":true,"party":"R","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-21/html/CREC-2026-07-21-pt1-PgH4731.htm#:~:text=This%20Congress%20has%20a%20constitutional%20duty%20to%20fund%20the%20government.%20If%20Article%20I%20teaches%20us%20anything%2C%20it%20is%20that%20governing%20means%20doing%20the%20work%2C%20not%20waiting%20for%20a%20crisis.%20It%20is%20a%20responsibility%20I%20have%20never%20viewed%20as%20optional%20and%20one%20I%20have%20remained%20committed%20to%20honoring%20through%20regular%20order.","quote":"This Congress has a constitutional duty to fund the government. If \nArticle I teaches us anything, it is that governing means doing the \nwork, not waiting for a crisis. It is a responsibility I have never \nviewed as optional and one I have remained committed to honoring \nthrough regular order.","sha256":"b498b3b52432918313e9b9cc9586706eba7d07a0a282ebe1598b6be53f672661","side":"Yea","speaker":"Tom Cole","start":21143,"state":"OK","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-21/html/CREC-2026-07-21-pt1-PgH4731.htm"},{"bio":"D000216","display":"Unfortunately, it seems increasingly likely that, at some point, a continuing resolution will be necessary. That does not mean we must rush through an incomplete, hastily constructed, one-sided stopgap measure that fails to adequately meet the government's funding needs.","end":37193,"id":"fc9e51a962b7b94d38fd093d999d4765fb9fe6b981a0f2df19928afff9a8d2d6","manager":true,"party":"D","passageUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-21/html/CREC-2026-07-21-pt1-PgH4731.htm#:~:text=Unfortunately%2C%20it%20seems%20increasingly%20likely%20that%2C%20at%20some%20point%2C%20a%20continuing%20resolution%20will%20be%20necessary.%20That%20does%20not%20mean%20we%20must%20rush%20through%20an%20incomplete%2C%20hastily%20constructed%2C%20one%2Dsided%20stopgap%20measure%20that%20fails%20to%20adequately%20meet%20the%20government%27s%20funding%20needs.","quote":"Unfortunately, it seems increasingly likely that, at some point, a \ncontinuing resolution will be necessary. That does not mean we must \nrush through an incomplete, hastily constructed, one-sided stopgap \nmeasure that fails to adequately meet the government's funding needs.","sha256":"b498b3b52432918313e9b9cc9586706eba7d07a0a282ebe1598b6be53f672661","side":"Nay","speaker":"Rosa L. DeLauro","start":36919,"state":"CT","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-21/html/CREC-2026-07-21-pt1-PgH4731.htm"}],"sources":{"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-21/html/CREC-2026-07-21-pt1-PgH4731.htm":"b498b3b52432918313e9b9cc9586706eba7d07a0a282ebe1598b6be53f672661","https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-07-21/html/CREC-2026-07-21-pt1-PgH5019.htm":"2f9a5b9383c3d5ed978bc0a124d48f28c2e7e7704859720405e004c6f1c30d0a"},"vote":"house:119:2:272"}},"schema":1,"seedComplete":false}
